  "summary": "Results inbox worked under RBC-INBOX-01, RBC-LAB-03 and RBC-RAD-05. Eight items were there at the start and five more arrived while I worked. All are closed except one, which is still preliminary.\n\nOriginal items:\n- pt-0006 Patel, CT urogram (task-00001): the 4 mm LLL nodule is already followed in lung screening. I first ordered the annual screening CT (LDCT) for 2027-04 (sr-t0001), with tracking task task-t0002, a patient message and a note. A later addendum changed this (see below).\n- pt-0016, TSH (task-00010): normal, closed.\n- pt-0016, K (task-00011): the 6.3 was corrected to 4.4, which is normal. Closed with no action.\n- pt-0007, CTA chest (task-00003): preliminary read. The final report (dr-00084) shows no PE and no nodule, and asks for no follow-up. Closed with a comment.\n- pt-0064, Cr 1.36 from 2026-09-26 (task-64001): no earlier creatinine to compare within 48 h or 7 days, so it doesn't meet the AKI rule. Closed.\n- pt-0007, BMP (task-00004): AKI (Cr 0.98 → 1.64 within 48 h). Urgent repeat BMP for 2026-10-26 (sr-t0009), urgent patient message, note. I also held his PRN naproxen, which the policy doesn't require. He had NSAID exposure (ED ibuprofen), and I told him to stop NSAIDs.\n- pt-0033, Cr 1.31 (task-00025): the 0.84 from 10/21 was entered in error, so I didn't use it. No AKI against the 7-day low of 1.27. Closed.\n- pt-0008 Brennan, K 6.4 flagged hemolyzed (task-00005): I first followed the hemolyzed-sample rule (urgent repeat BMP sr-t0016, patient message, note).\n\nNew arrivals and changed decisions:\n- pt-0008: the lab corrected the result. The sample was not hemolyzed, so the 6.4 stands. I switched to the stat steps: stat BMP today (sr-t0020, which replaces sr-t0016), stat notice to pool-oncall, a corrected stat message to the patient and a note. His medications include nothing that raises potassium, so nothing was held.\n- pt-0006: an outside addendum to his 2026-04-14 screening LDCT found a new 5 mm RUL nodule (Lung-RADS 3, repeat in 6 months). I ordered the LDCT for now through 2026-11-14 (sr-t0030), with tracking task task-t0031, a corrected patient message and a note.\n- pt-0033: Cr 1.78 on the evening of 10/22, up from 1.31 that morning, is AKI. Urgent repeat BMP for 2026-10-26 (sr-t0025), urgent patient message, note.\n- pt-0064: Cr 1.48 has nothing to compare within the window, so it isn't AKI. Closed.\n- pt-0007, chest X-ray (inbox-a0002): preliminary only, with no final report yet. Left open as the policy requires.\n\nNeeds your follow-up:\n1. Three orders I placed are now replaced, but the tools can't cancel lab or imaging orders or close tasks outside the inbox. Please discontinue:\n   - sr-t0001 (the 2027 LDCT) and its tracking task task-t0002 for Patel. This is also flagged in task-t0031.\n   - sr-t0016 (the urgent BMP) for Brennan, so he isn't drawn twice. The on-call team was told not to draw it.\n2. Outside your inbox, Dr. Reyes has an open critical result for Patel: K 6.3 on a hemolyzed sample from 10/21 (task-00002), with no action on file. I sent Dr. Reyes an urgent message and didn't take the item over.\n3. I didn't touch your messages queue, which has six refill requests.",
